update the app tests for the panel-sized canvas and whole-texture source

Five tests in crates/slot/tests/app.rs failed on every build of this port
since the patches that changed what they measure, while upstream's own
suite passed. They were never wrong about behaviour; they were written
against upstream's 720x480 canvas and its cropping stretch.

  - 0002 makes the canvas the 752x560 panel. The core picker's lid
    shadow was expected at x=360, the Cancel hint at x=234, and the board
    to rise downwards between its start and rest positions. On the
    taller canvas the board rises (y 174 to 150), the shadow centres on
    the canvas, and Cancel sits beside Swap, which the test already
    checks. They derive from the canvas now.

  - 0009 makes source_rect the whole texture in both modes, and sizes
    the stretched picture through game_base instead. The two stretch
    tests looked for the old crop window. They compare game_base with
    base_size for a stretched Game Boy.

Test changes only. Applies after 0026.

